1
00:00:02,880 --> 00:01:57,930
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:02,160
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:15,510
Clear the way! Get out of the way!

4
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:23,620
Clear the way! Get out of the way!

5
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,070
Answer my questions.

6
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:35,970
That you've saved my life doesn't matter,
I can still kill you.

7
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:38,170
What are you doing here?

8
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:43,040
Did you kill the Governor?

9
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:48,150
What Governor? What are you talking about?

10
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:54,070
As a Turk, what are you doing here?

11
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:14,790
You nearly killed him.

12
00:03:17,810 --> 00:03:20,550
Ertuğrul's son Osman.

13
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:28,610
What the hell are you doing?
How did you come up here?

14
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:42,190
Ertuğrul Bey's son, the famous Osman, huh?

15
00:03:43,850 --> 00:03:46,170
He is skillful like his father.

16
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:54,950
They say, "A wolf's offspring becomes
another wolf."

17
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:03,750
Do what you have to do.
I'll take care of him.

18
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:49,710
Job 26:7 [ Bible verse ]

19
00:04:51,490 --> 00:04:54,070
Job 26:7 [ Bible verse ]

20
00:04:55,750 --> 00:05:01,150
"He puts north in nothingness."

21
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:05,740
"He drops the earth in...

22
00:05:08,970 --> 00:05:10,830
nothingness."

23
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:24,860
148:3

24
00:05:26,010 --> 00:05:27,980
"Glorify him."

25
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:35,730
"The sun and the moon,
all the gleaming stars."

26
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:46,850
104:6

27
00:05:47,590 --> 00:05:52,060
"He wore the headwaters like a dress."

28
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:57,850
"And the water was standing
on the top of the mountains"

29
00:06:44,030 --> 00:06:46,270
Absolute thanks to my Lord.

30
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:48,810
Allah is the greatest.

31
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:51,530
Allah is the greatest.

32
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:53,900
Allah is the greatest.

33
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:59,450
We also need to find
what our master mentioned.

34
00:07:11,850 --> 00:07:13,550
I've found it.

35
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:25,730
IN THE NAME OF ALLAH THE MERCIFUL.

36
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:47,050
"Indeed, We have given you,
[O Muhammad], a clear conquest"
Surah Al-Fath [48:1]

37
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,950
Thank Allah.

38
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,100
Thank Allah.

39
00:07:54,710 --> 00:07:57,450
Now that the Governor is dead,
there must be a panic.

40
00:07:57,510 --> 00:08:01,180
We don't have much time. Come on,
hurry up. We need to take him out now.

41
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:03,220
Ya Bismillah! ( in the name of Allah.)

42
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:17,520
You couldn't protect your Governor.

43
00:08:19,850 --> 00:08:22,620
You turned his castle into
a grave for him.

44
00:08:23,290 --> 00:08:27,290
Damn you, Commanders.

45
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:32,680
None of you have been like Osman.

46
00:08:33,810 --> 00:08:35,770
Damn it.

47
00:08:38,190 --> 00:08:39,960
Answer me!

48
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,930
How could you not take precautions?

49
00:08:44,130 --> 00:08:45,700
How could you not!

50
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:51,020
In this castle, there is no traitor
who means to kill our Governor.

51
00:08:52,190 --> 00:08:55,070
We were his sons.

52
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:58,380
We would risk our lives for him.

53
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:03,250
We'll question everyone in the castle.
We'll make everyone talk.

54
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:05,910
Where was the Governor?

55
00:09:05,910 --> 00:09:08,290
With whom was he?
We'll learn everything.

56
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:11,130
He was in his room.

57
00:09:12,270 --> 00:09:15,560
I sent Helen to his room to call him.

58
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:22,300
After I notified our Governor with
our offer, he took action.

59
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:29,790
But, before I went into his room, I saw
Ertuğrul's son Osman leaving his room.

60
00:09:30,450 --> 00:09:32,160
What did you say?

61
00:09:32,510 --> 00:09:35,180
- Are you sure that he was Osman?
- Yes, sir.

62
00:09:35,250 --> 00:09:37,680
It was Ertuğrul's son Osman.

63
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:39,320
Osman...

64
00:09:42,410 --> 00:09:45,600
Search the whole castle right away,
Andreas.

65
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,710
Get all the Commanders into the act!

66
00:09:47,710 --> 00:09:49,790
Search for the whole castle!

67
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:21,910
Come on.
I hear footsteps.

68
00:10:22,670 --> 00:10:25,830
Don't worry.
He'll wake up soon.

69
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:29,100
He has a heart that could dare
all the world.

70
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:32,020
He'll take care of himself.
Let's go.

71
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:02,560
You're entrusted to Allah.

72
00:11:04,870 --> 00:11:06,390
Let's go!

73
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:11,600
Come on, come on, hurry up!
Run! Hurry up!

74
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:46,480
Inform the Commanders.
Osman is in the castle.

75
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:10,770
I promise you I will find Osman,
and we will be settled down.

76
00:13:21,650 --> 00:13:25,970
I told you the stars would
help us tonight.

77
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,910
Commander Kalonoz, Commander Kalonoz!

78
00:13:31,770 --> 00:13:33,840
Osman is in the Sofia's starry room!

79
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,790
- Starry room?
- I'll catch him, Sofia.

80
00:13:40,230 --> 00:13:42,460
What is Osman doing there?

81
00:13:42,930 --> 00:13:44,970
The holy entrustment!

82
00:14:18,370 --> 00:14:21,300
You killed our Governor, you bastard!

83
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:25,810
The killer of the Governor
is the most innocent one of you.

84
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:00,020
Run! Catch Osman!

85
00:15:00,330 --> 00:15:03,750
Catch him before he exits the castle!

86
00:15:37,690 --> 00:15:40,090
Damn it, we missed him!

87
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:44,760
The Governor is dead!

88
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:50,890
Where are you, my Bey?

89
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,610
Where are you, my Bey?

90
00:16:04,890 --> 00:16:06,610
My Bey.

91
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:10,630
My Bey, drink water.
Catch your breath.

92
00:16:14,590 --> 00:16:17,110
I worried about you when the bells ringed.

93
00:16:17,110 --> 00:16:19,980
The governor is dead, I am held
responsible for it.

94
00:16:20,030 --> 00:16:21,860
What are you talking about, my Bey?

95
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:25,270
We need to find somewhere to hide
immediately.

96
00:16:25,270 --> 00:16:28,530
Let's go to Mario's place, my Bey.

97
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:33,510
You thought it well. Don't let anyone
stop you, kill them all!

98
00:16:33,510 --> 00:16:35,420
- Okay.
- Let's go!

99
00:17:02,610 --> 00:17:05,730
They took the holy entrustment and the
treasure!

100
00:17:06,190 --> 00:17:07,830
Damn it!

101
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:13,800
Forgive my sins, god.

102
00:17:15,190 --> 00:17:17,990
Inform Master Yannis right away.

103
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:23,540
Sofia, Master Yannis would make both
of us pay for this.

104
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:33,760
How could we explain this to Master
Yannis, huh?

105
00:17:35,810 --> 00:17:39,950
We couldn't enjoy the governor's
death, now we sorrow for this.

106
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,050
Osman.

107
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:50,820
I'll bite your lungs out with my teeth.

108
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,000
Osman!

109
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:14,080
Apparently, no one saw us.
Nobody is around.

110
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:17,050
I'll pray to thank to Allah when we
arrive in our city.

111
00:18:17,050 --> 00:18:19,690
You need to depart early in the morning.

112
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:22,800
Won't you come?

113
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:26,040
The war has just started, daughter.

114
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:29,890
The ones who serve to the devil will
take action.

115
00:18:29,890 --> 00:18:33,620
The Governor has been killed, things will
go crazy here.

116
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:35,390
Do you think Osman is okay?

117
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,400
What if he couldn't get out?

118
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,840
Thank my Lord.

119
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:50,090
We have found Ahi Evren's treasure, which
was kept by the enemy.

120
00:18:50,550 --> 00:18:54,360
We have the blessed treasure of
Ahmad Yasawi.

121
00:18:54,510 --> 00:18:56,390
Thank Lord.

122
00:19:28,190 --> 00:19:31,840
I wonder, my Bey.
Who do you think killed the Governor?

123
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:33,920
I don't know, brother.

124
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:35,910
I don't know.

125
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:41,100
However, I know something.
The Governor was killed by his closest ones.

126
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:44,120
You are right, my Bey.

127
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:46,490
Governor nursed vipers in his bosom.

128
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:48,480
Why did they kill him?

129
00:19:48,570 --> 00:19:51,830
Because he made peace with us.
They couldn't accept this.

130
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:55,800
They want to end the peace and
fight again.

131
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:57,790
Who are those bastards, my Bey?

132
00:19:57,790 --> 00:20:01,450
As they arranged such an ignominious
assassinate...

133
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:04,820
It must be a secret organization.

134
00:20:05,050 --> 00:20:09,710
A secret organization that is everywhere
in Bithynia

135
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:12,770
They took advantage of the fact that my
father is in Konya.

136
00:20:12,770 --> 00:20:16,540
- We should send men to the tribe, my Bey.
- Kalonoz must have done it already.

137
00:20:17,210 --> 00:20:20,330
Their aim is to disorder the tent
by using me.

138
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:25,420
My brothers, we are under attack
from two sides.

139
00:20:28,910 --> 00:20:31,380
The woman who masqueraded as a
priestess...

140
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:33,840
She is our salvation.

141
00:20:34,170 --> 00:20:37,450
If we find her, we'll find both
the murderer of the Governor and...

142
00:20:37,450 --> 00:20:38,990
the traitors in the castle.

143
00:20:48,730 --> 00:20:53,330
- Did you that devil?
- The ground swallowed him up, dajjal Turk!

144
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:57,640
Unless you find Osman, we can't breathe
in this land!

145
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:59,280
I'll find him.

146
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:03,130
Swear to god, I'll find and kill him
myself!

147
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:06,830
It's not easy to find him.

148
00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:10,720
- He must come with his will.
- How?

149
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:16,500
He is a Turk who risked his life
for the Governor.

150
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:22,640
If we capture someone from his blood...

151
00:21:23,250 --> 00:21:27,670
he'll give in to save him.

152
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:32,250
Devil took the possession of the whole
castle tonight.

153
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:40,620
Sometimes you need to get help from
the devil to keep up.

154
00:21:53,710 --> 00:21:56,890
We'll take an entrustment from Dündar Bey.

155
00:21:57,440 --> 00:22:03,190
And that entrustment will make Osman
be revealed.

156
00:22:03,290 --> 00:22:08,790
And because of Osman, the tent
will be troubled.

157
00:22:12,070 --> 00:22:14,680
I'll send my most trusted man.

158
00:22:16,980 --> 00:22:20,090
Dündar Bey is going to be mad about this.

159
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:22,780
And the agreement will be infringed.

160
00:22:25,850 --> 00:22:27,740
Ertuğrul's son Osman...

161
00:22:28,550 --> 00:22:34,600
who killed our Governor has infringed
the agreement.

162
00:22:41,490 --> 00:22:47,040
Everyone should hear and believe that
Osman has committed this murder.

163
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:53,750
Everyone should know how Kayıs treat
their friends.

164
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:24,590
- Can I, Uncle?
- Come in, Gündüz Bey.

165
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:30,290
Is there any news from Osman?

166
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:36,920
We searched everywhere, uncle.
But, nothing is up.

167
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:41,730
I don't understand what his aim is.

168
00:23:41,780 --> 00:23:45,880
Sometimes he saves the day...

169
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:50,360
sometimes he spoils the day.

170
00:23:53,430 --> 00:23:56,550
This has gone too far, Dündar Bey.

171
00:23:56,550 --> 00:23:59,260
Ertuğrul Ghazi should know what happened.

172
00:24:00,300 --> 00:24:06,260
You should send a letter that tells what
happened in the tent, Dündar Bey.

173
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:10,210
You need to report Osman's situation.

174
00:24:10,230 --> 00:24:16,610
My aunt is right. What would we do if my
father came to the tent and asked...

175
00:24:16,610 --> 00:24:20,560
where Osman is?

176
00:24:31,390 --> 00:24:34,450
Ahh, Osman, ah.

177
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:37,690
Look what you've done to me.

178
00:24:38,370 --> 00:24:42,840
But, you gave me no option.

179
00:24:44,850 --> 00:24:46,770
You didn't.

180
00:24:55,680 --> 00:25:00,220
- Selamun Aleikum, Dündar Bey.
- Aleikum Selam, Bamsı Bey.

181
00:25:01,310 --> 00:25:04,150
- Here, sit down.
- Thank you.

182
00:25:17,460 --> 00:25:19,720
Long live, Dündar Bey.

183
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:35,810
Osman, Dündar Bey, where is he?

184
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:40,680
It's been a while, but Osman is not
around.

185
00:25:42,130 --> 00:25:45,890
The enemy is waiting for a gap.

186
00:25:46,540 --> 00:25:51,570
What if they hunt Osman down, like my
Aybars?

187
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:55,490
We were going to ask you, Bamsı Bey.

188
00:25:55,520 --> 00:25:59,420
I am not Bey, son.
The Bey is Dündar Bey.

189
00:25:59,580 --> 00:26:03,830
He needs to know what is going on.

190
00:26:08,220 --> 00:26:13,490
If something happens to Osman, how can you
explain it to my Ertuğrul Bey, huh?

191
00:26:14,910 --> 00:26:16,330
Huh?

192
00:26:16,330 --> 00:26:18,380
Brother Gündüz?

193
00:26:20,210 --> 00:26:21,450
Huh?

194
00:26:21,870 --> 00:26:23,740
Uncle Dündar?

195
00:26:25,700 --> 00:26:27,010
Bey.

196
00:26:38,730 --> 00:26:43,330
I wish my Ertuğrul Bey had come so that...

197
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:48,550
the tent could be in order.

198
00:27:12,070 --> 00:27:18,840
Send Alps (men) for Osman, Gündüz Bey.
They shall not come back without his trace.

199
00:27:30,940 --> 00:27:33,310
Will you send the letter, my Bey?

200
00:27:39,250 --> 00:27:41,030
My Bey, I'm talking to you.

201
00:27:42,890 --> 00:27:45,030
What should I tell to my brother, huh?

202
00:27:45,310 --> 00:27:49,840
What should I tell? Should I tell him that
I couldn't take care of Osman?

203
00:27:50,520 --> 00:27:53,400
Won't he ask me that how will you deal
with the tent...

204
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:56,050
while you can't even take care of Osman?

205
00:28:59,450 --> 00:29:01,580
Is Governor Yorgopolos dead?

206
00:29:01,730 --> 00:29:03,270
Yes, sir.

207
00:29:03,890 --> 00:29:08,410
So, why are you silent as the snow on the
Olympios Mountains, Megela?

208
00:29:08,410 --> 00:29:11,560
Sir, the runner that Sofia sent brought
you a letter.

209
00:29:11,560 --> 00:29:12,930
Read it.

210
00:29:23,660 --> 00:29:27,460
Read, Megela, read!
What is written in the letter?

211
00:29:32,170 --> 00:29:33,800
Sir...

212
00:29:35,990 --> 00:29:39,720
The holy entrustment and the treasure are
stolen from the sorcery room.

213
00:29:40,060 --> 00:29:41,980
It happened in the Yorgopolos' scene.

214
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:46,770
Who did know the place of the room that
the secret is hidden, huh?

215
00:29:46,770 --> 00:29:48,940
How did they learn this, Megela, how?

216
00:29:50,390 --> 00:29:53,900
- Who did this?
- Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman.

217
00:29:56,790 --> 00:30:00,970
A shepherd Turk has spoiled everything!

218
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:06,870
Osman, Osman, Osman...

219
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:11,150
Get my horse ready, we are going to
Kulucahisar Castle

220
00:30:11,150 --> 00:30:12,940
Yes, sir.

221
00:30:23,520 --> 00:30:27,570
What happened to this store?
Everything's messed up.

222
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:29,460
Ugh!

223
00:30:30,450 --> 00:30:33,630
You can't even rely on your helpmate.

224
00:30:33,770 --> 00:30:36,010
God damn you all!

225
00:30:38,160 --> 00:30:41,120
Who are you?
What are you looking for?

226
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:45,560
Don't take it personally, man.
You'll work for us today.

227
00:30:54,030 --> 00:30:55,800
Let's finish this.

228
00:30:55,820 --> 00:30:57,360
Okay, my Bey.

229
00:31:29,970 --> 00:31:31,770
The carriage is ready.

230
00:31:32,230 --> 00:31:34,360
It is time to depart.

231
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:36,790
They'll wait for you outside of the
castle.

232
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:40,630
I charged the soldiers in the gate.

233
00:31:41,040 --> 00:31:44,820
If someone asks you something,
don't talk.

234
00:31:44,870 --> 00:31:47,170
Those soldiers will save you.

235
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:50,900
May Allah help you, Dursun Bey.

236
00:31:51,500 --> 00:31:54,850
May my Lord make you the victorious
in this cruel land.

237
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:57,150
Thank you, daughter.

238
00:31:58,220 --> 00:31:59,870
Thank you.

239
00:32:03,110 --> 00:32:07,110
I respectfully kiss my
master's blessed hands.

240
00:32:08,590 --> 00:32:12,250
I hope he wouldn't forsake his
prayers from this poor man.

241
00:32:12,500 --> 00:32:17,130
Tell him we need his favour and breath.

242
00:32:25,580 --> 00:32:26,880
Master Dursun.

243
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:31,470
Is there any news about Osman?

244
00:32:39,330 --> 00:32:42,790
He is missing, for now.

245
00:32:43,780 --> 00:32:46,250
He is Osman, son of Ertuğrul.

246
00:32:47,220 --> 00:32:51,220
No one could know where
and when he could show up.

247
00:33:01,030 --> 00:33:05,030
- May Allah help you, Dursun Bey.
- Amen.

248
00:33:07,780 --> 00:33:10,780
May Allah help you.

249
00:33:24,100 --> 00:33:25,460
Folks!

250
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:32,490
Last night, our governor,
Yorgopolos was murdered!

251
00:33:34,710 --> 00:33:37,960
May God take him to his heaven.

252
00:33:39,180 --> 00:33:46,340
The killer of our governor is Osman Bey,
son of Ertuğrul from the Kayıs!

253
00:33:48,190 --> 00:33:52,190
The killer of our governor is Osman Bey!

254
00:33:54,910 --> 00:33:58,530
We know that the killer is in our castle.

255
00:33:58,650 --> 00:34:04,790
Whoever helps him,
dies with the whole family!

256
00:34:07,500 --> 00:34:12,370
Our governor, Yorgopolos was murdered!

257
00:34:12,570 --> 00:34:14,310
Driver, stop!

258
00:34:34,090 --> 00:34:37,140
- What's in the cart?
- It's extra-virgin olive oil.

259
00:34:37,210 --> 00:34:39,850
Good, open it so we can see then.

260
00:34:45,280 --> 00:34:49,280
It can't have sunlight,
they will be wasted, soldier.

261
00:34:49,350 --> 00:34:50,850
- It's olive oil-
- Enough!

262
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:54,390
- You'll make me starve in winter.
- I said open it!

263
00:34:56,900 --> 00:34:59,960
Please, I'm going to be
hungry with my children.

264
00:35:00,020 --> 00:35:04,020
Just leave it, are we going to find
Osman in a barrel of olive oil?

265
00:35:05,570 --> 00:35:08,960
- Come on.
- What are you waiting for, move!

266
00:35:12,180 --> 00:35:14,970
May God spare you for your children.

267
00:35:27,310 --> 00:35:28,830
Open the gate!

268
00:35:47,440 --> 00:35:50,630
Thank you, my Allah! Victory is ours!

269
00:36:29,540 --> 00:36:32,340
We are near the church, my Bey.
Shall we come with you?

270
00:36:32,580 --> 00:36:37,330
You do as I ordered, I will enter
the church alone, I will see you soon.

271
00:37:15,050 --> 00:37:17,470
Greetings, Priest.

272
00:37:22,840 --> 00:37:26,840
Welcome to the house of God,
strong warrior of Jesus Christ.

273
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:29,310
I wish everyone...

274
00:37:30,150 --> 00:37:35,090
... could have the strength to handle
the hardships like our Lord Jesus Christ.

275
00:37:35,460 --> 00:37:39,460
All prophets are embodiments of faith.

276
00:37:41,480 --> 00:37:45,480
It is not easy to be
like our Lord Jesus Christ.

277
00:37:49,290 --> 00:37:54,520
How lucky you are, Master Priest, to spend
your life in a sanctuary like this...

278
00:37:55,660 --> 00:37:59,660
... away from all the
sins, the filth out there.

279
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:07,260
- This is the first time I see you here.
- Because it's my first time here.

280
00:38:08,940 --> 00:38:12,240
Do you know the face of
everyone from your community?

281
00:38:12,510 --> 00:38:15,980
Our church community is fewer in this age.

282
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:20,720
Most of them chose to become
a Muslim because of the Turks.

283
00:38:21,160 --> 00:38:27,640
Old people usually visit here, but when
I see younglings, I don't let them go.

284
00:38:28,570 --> 00:38:32,790
- That's why I couldn't recognize you.
- I'm looking for a nun.

285
00:38:33,970 --> 00:38:36,930
She is a very important person for me.

286
00:38:37,660 --> 00:38:40,620
If you tell me her name, maybe I can help.

287
00:38:40,800 --> 00:38:43,000
I don't know her name.

288
00:38:43,730 --> 00:38:47,730
How could I help you
if you don't know her name?

289
00:38:49,770 --> 00:38:53,050
Black eyebrows, hazel eyes...

290
00:38:54,650 --> 00:38:56,920
... about this height.

291
00:38:58,150 --> 00:39:02,150
Son, there must be so many
nuns with these descriptions...

292
00:39:03,760 --> 00:39:07,760
What is that secret of her that
made you chase after this nun?

293
00:39:08,130 --> 00:39:09,720
I owe her my life.

294
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,500
I'd like to pay my debt.

295
00:39:16,710 --> 00:39:20,710
Does she have little freckles on her face?

296
00:39:32,070 --> 00:39:33,100
Yes.

297
00:39:35,120 --> 00:39:39,120
You're talking about our church's mary
Nevodaka.

298
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:45,000
She lives in a shrine out of the city.
I will describe the place for you.

299
00:39:45,490 --> 00:39:46,930
Are you sure?

300
00:39:47,250 --> 00:39:50,410
Look, son. Listen to me carefully now.

301
00:40:53,400 --> 00:40:54,820
Burçin.

302
00:41:08,370 --> 00:41:09,990
Enough!

303
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:14,840
Don't you see the rage
inside you poisons you too?

304
00:41:14,930 --> 00:41:20,370
First Aybars, now his men. Who knows to
what trouble he dragged them now.

305
00:41:21,350 --> 00:41:24,300
This tent lost its soul,
it's happiness because of him.

306
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:27,790
Who knows how many men
will die because of him, Aygül!

307
00:41:32,790 --> 00:41:37,000
And you are still worried
about him. Thinking about him.

308
00:41:37,650 --> 00:41:41,970
Don't you know how Osman
is poisoning you in the first place?

309
00:41:42,170 --> 00:41:46,390
One day, you will also be in
big trouble because of him.

310
00:41:47,530 --> 00:41:51,530
I know you are hurt.

311
00:41:52,580 --> 00:41:56,580
You feel the pain in your bones.

312
00:41:57,010 --> 00:42:01,850
But you put the blame on Osman,
forgetting about the will of Allah.

313
00:42:04,020 --> 00:42:08,020
I will regard the trouble coming
from Osman as an honour!

314
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:11,420
You should know that.

315
00:42:12,980 --> 00:42:16,980
Of course, I know that.
My Aybars is a martyr.

316
00:42:18,760 --> 00:42:22,390
But this doesn't explain
Osman's recklessness!

317
00:42:23,070 --> 00:42:30,770
No need to talk more, if your heart burns
like mine does now, you will understand.

318
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:34,060
Good day to you!

319
00:42:34,940 --> 00:42:37,420
Burçin Hatun! Burçin Hatun!

320
00:42:39,900 --> 00:42:41,510
Don't come.

321
00:43:36,450 --> 00:43:41,070
There, Dündar's daughter, let's finish
this before the guards notice anything.

322
00:43:41,820 --> 00:43:43,020
Come on.

323
00:43:55,360 --> 00:43:57,710
You still hate Osman.

324
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:06,480
Don't forget that he went to
avenge the man you loved.

325
00:44:06,970 --> 00:44:09,380
He took my lover from me, Aygül.

326
00:44:10,590 --> 00:44:12,830
You are still talking about revenge.

327
00:44:14,050 --> 00:44:18,050
He will burn your heart
just like he has burnt mine.

328
00:44:28,520 --> 00:44:31,770
What do you want?
What are you doing here?

329
00:44:31,860 --> 00:44:34,370
Osman killed our governor.

330
00:44:35,970 --> 00:44:41,140
He is trapped in the castle like a rat. We
need bait to lure him out of his hole.

331
00:44:42,740 --> 00:44:45,210
And that bait is you, Aygül Hatun!

332
00:45:40,920 --> 00:45:44,920
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

333
00:45:45,550 --> 00:45:49,000
With the Almighty Allah's 99 names,
who creates everything with "be"...

334
00:45:49,090 --> 00:45:54,300
... who fills our hearts with faith.

335
00:45:59,230 --> 00:46:02,880
Brave men of the Great Oğuz.

336
00:46:04,030 --> 00:46:08,030
You all know about the
circumstances in Bithynia.

337
00:46:08,610 --> 00:46:13,000
These lands that we come in with
my brother, Ertuğrul Gazi's leadership...

338
00:46:13,590 --> 00:46:16,430
... hide their fruitful face from us.

339
00:46:17,180 --> 00:46:20,670
It can't carry our weight anymore.

340
00:46:21,670 --> 00:46:28,160
After all this time, both our tents
and our herds grew in number.

341
00:46:29,460 --> 00:46:34,870
There are many problems appearing
in every tent, every tribe.

342
00:46:35,520 --> 00:46:41,730
Some of us are far from the water,
some of us lack the pasture.

343
00:46:42,060 --> 00:46:46,670
And there are bandits,
caravan ambushers, too.

344
00:46:47,890 --> 00:46:54,800
Because of all these reasons, we have been
searching for a remedy for our troubles.

345
00:46:56,230 --> 00:47:00,500
This remedy is alliance.

346
00:47:01,100 --> 00:47:02,580
[Man 2] That's right.

347
00:47:05,930 --> 00:47:08,740
Thus, we have signed a trade
agreement...

348
00:47:09,020 --> 00:47:13,920
... with our neighbour Yorgopolos,
the Governor of Kulucahisar.

349
00:47:14,890 --> 00:47:19,060
Both them and we will be the winners.

350
00:47:20,590 --> 00:47:26,510
Our goods will be sold in Yenipazar
too, in addition to Söğüt.

351
00:47:35,470 --> 00:47:40,030
What is it, Samsa Bey? You don't seem
to be happy with the results.

352
00:47:43,230 --> 00:47:47,230
Dündar Bey, you say my brother but...

353
00:47:48,770 --> 00:47:52,610
... Ertuğrul Gazi didn't come to
this land calculating incomes.

354
00:47:53,340 --> 00:47:58,650
And he brought us to strike to the
infidels' hearts, not to loot.

355
00:47:59,990 --> 00:48:06,040
Moreover, we've come here to put the
world in order under the wolf banner...

356
00:48:06,040 --> 00:48:08,690
... not to ride caravans!

357
00:48:10,850 --> 00:48:15,710
Also, we can't be friends with infidels.

358
00:48:22,250 --> 00:48:24,920
Brave Bey of Kayı!

359
00:48:26,400 --> 00:48:32,020
I know how you are thrilled when
you hear about the war and fight.

360
00:48:33,530 --> 00:48:38,310
But don't you forget that lands
can be taken with weapons but...

361
00:48:39,030 --> 00:48:42,840
... order can not be
established with weapons.

362
00:48:44,810 --> 00:48:52,230
Order needs coin, wisdom, and skill.

363
00:48:55,120 --> 00:48:58,610
Samsa wants nothing but war, Dündar Bey.

364
00:48:58,780 --> 00:49:02,780
You need order, not war, Nizam Bey.

365
00:49:03,330 --> 00:49:10,160
Ovens become home, homes
become tents, tents become a country.

366
00:49:11,700 --> 00:49:16,580
I've told you so many times to
let us marry you, you didn't want it.

367
00:49:31,310 --> 00:49:35,310
I have been fighting since
I put this black weapon on my belt.

368
00:49:37,410 --> 00:49:41,410
I called bed to eagle nests,
I called blanket to the sky.

369
00:49:41,750 --> 00:49:45,530
I became friends with
hawks, allied with wolves.

370
00:49:45,760 --> 00:49:48,410
I know about your greatness
and virtue, Dündar Bey.

371
00:49:48,870 --> 00:49:51,910
But the only friend or lover
of Samsa, who can't stand still...

372
00:49:52,070 --> 00:49:56,070
... when he hears about fighting,
is this weapon.

373
00:49:59,440 --> 00:50:01,260
Let it be known like this.

374
00:50:03,620 --> 00:50:08,320
I've made my promise, I made my
oaths, my marriage is with this.

375
00:50:10,430 --> 00:50:13,690
And my wedding is with death.

376
00:51:02,480 --> 00:51:05,110
Just because we've formed
an alliance doesn't mean...

377
00:51:05,340 --> 00:51:07,900
... we've left our weapons
like that, Samsa Bey.

378
00:51:09,790 --> 00:51:15,750
Don't you worry, our agreement with
the governor will bring peace to everyone.

379
00:51:16,070 --> 00:51:19,860
There is no peace in a place where
we aren't present Gündüz Bey.

380
00:51:22,180 --> 00:51:24,470
Haven't you figured it out yet?

381
00:51:31,320 --> 00:51:37,300
You blow like the wind and
help us breathe, welcome, Alişar Bey.

382
00:51:45,960 --> 00:51:49,690
Thank you, but we didn't
hear good news, Dündar Bey.

383
00:51:52,470 --> 00:51:57,140
You made an agreement with the governor
without informing the banner lord.

384
00:52:11,570 --> 00:52:17,750
All these tribes, tents, how
did you manage to settle here?

385
00:52:18,800 --> 00:52:22,800
Don't you know I am the shadow
of the Sultan in these lands?

386
00:52:25,170 --> 00:52:28,520
Don't you worry, Alişar Bey.

387
00:52:28,740 --> 00:52:32,740
We surely do not forget
about the order, the respect.

388
00:52:39,430 --> 00:52:43,430
Your door is not the door of wrongs...

389
00:52:44,550 --> 00:52:47,440
... but the door of
rightfulness, Alişar Bey.

390
00:52:47,870 --> 00:52:53,090
We were going to knock on your door after
we are cleaned from our flaws but...

391
00:52:53,970 --> 00:52:56,130
... you were ahead of us.

392
00:52:58,750 --> 00:53:00,940
Let me go! I will see Dündar Bey!

393
00:53:00,980 --> 00:53:03,120
What is going on there?

394
00:53:04,570 --> 00:53:06,380
- Dündar Bey!
- Burçin!

395
00:53:07,340 --> 00:53:09,390
Burçin, my girl! Burçin, my girl!

396
00:53:09,500 --> 00:53:12,400
- What is it? What happened to you?
- Who did this to you?

397
00:53:12,640 --> 00:53:17,520
Drink water. You should
drink water. Who laid their hands on you?

398
00:53:20,660 --> 00:53:24,050
Father! Andreas, commander of Kalonoz.

399
00:53:24,570 --> 00:53:27,420
- They kidnapped Aygül.
- What are you talking about, girl?

400
00:53:27,570 --> 00:53:28,930
How dare them?

401
00:53:29,060 --> 00:53:30,970
Where did they kidnap her, speak!

402
00:53:31,120 --> 00:53:33,750
They ambushed us while
we were doing laundry, my Bey.

403
00:53:33,850 --> 00:53:36,710
They abducted Aygül,
then let me go so I can tell you.

404
00:53:36,980 --> 00:53:40,710
What do they want? Speak, girl.
What do they want?

405
00:53:40,780 --> 00:53:46,010
Osman. They want Osman.
They ask for you for this reason.

406
00:53:46,680 --> 00:53:50,250
- Osman?
- Osman killed the governor.

407
00:53:50,930 --> 00:53:55,810
They are searching for him in the castle.
They took Aygül hostage to find Osman.

408
00:54:03,610 --> 00:54:08,420
My Osman, my Osman went
to the castle to find Aybars' killers.

409
00:54:09,220 --> 00:54:14,350
Dündar Bey, clearly Osman has something,
that's why they are searching for him.

410
00:54:14,810 --> 00:54:18,330
We should go to the castle
before anything happens to Aygül!

411
00:54:18,470 --> 00:54:23,660
Gündüz, you prepare for war with the Beys,
we are going to the castle with Bamsı Bey.

412
00:54:23,900 --> 00:54:26,420
If we don't come back from that castle...

413
00:54:26,510 --> 00:54:30,510
Leave no stone unturned,
leave no shoulder with a head.

414
00:54:32,260 --> 00:54:37,560
I told you, we can't be friends with
infidels. No time to wait, I'm coming too.

415
00:54:37,750 --> 00:54:42,620
You know the best about
the infidels, let's go then.

416
00:54:43,310 --> 00:54:44,690
Dündar Bey.

417
00:54:46,810 --> 00:54:50,090
Where are you going
without the banner lord?

418
00:54:50,790 --> 00:54:54,790
We should take our precautions
first, inform our Sultan.

419
00:54:55,520 --> 00:55:00,870
We wash honour with life,
and blood with blood.

420
00:55:00,960 --> 00:55:05,590
I don't have time to wait.
You do your duty as the banner lord...

421
00:55:06,370 --> 00:55:11,250
... and I will do what needs to
be done as a father and an uncle.

422
00:55:12,410 --> 00:55:13,720
Excuse us.

423
00:55:33,850 --> 00:55:37,850
Look at this hunter of Kayı, Osman...

424
00:55:38,290 --> 00:55:41,360
... I've never seen him
miss his target in our hunts.

425
00:55:41,540 --> 00:55:45,540
He must have tracked
the killer of Aybars carefully.

426
00:55:45,780 --> 00:55:49,780
Let's see what is going to happen now.

427
00:55:59,680 --> 00:56:02,660
Our way is clear from now on.

428
00:56:02,790 --> 00:56:06,210
The information we will get
from the places we will go to...

429
00:56:06,410 --> 00:56:08,730
... will lead us to my
brother Aybar's killers.

430
00:56:08,840 --> 00:56:11,030
Osman, son of Ertuğrul Bey!

431
00:56:12,430 --> 00:56:15,720
I know you are in the
castle and you can hear me!

432
00:56:19,230 --> 00:56:21,770
And I know you killed the governor!

433
00:56:23,120 --> 00:56:24,020
Aygül!

434
00:56:26,260 --> 00:56:28,450
We have witnesses!

435
00:56:35,350 --> 00:56:38,640
We have the daughter of Dündar Bey, Aygül!

436
00:56:39,670 --> 00:56:43,670
I give you one last chance to surrender!

437
00:56:44,780 --> 00:56:51,670
Surrender to Commander Kalonoz now, or the
daughter of Dündar Bey will be killed!

438
00:56:54,020 --> 00:56:59,690
We also send word to Dündar Bey, he will
come to the castle for his daughter!

439
00:57:00,920 --> 00:57:04,920
If you don't surrender, we will
also kill him when he comes!

440
00:57:14,530 --> 00:57:17,480
Tell Osman to come and surrender.

441
00:57:19,270 --> 00:57:20,090
Get up!

442
00:57:39,590 --> 00:57:44,710
Osman! Don't you surrender, Osman!

443
00:57:46,520 --> 00:57:48,300
Shut your mouth!

444
00:57:53,690 --> 00:57:58,210
My Bey, this is not the time for
anger, we need to act now.

445
00:58:00,730 --> 00:58:03,540
Osman this is your last warning from me!

446
00:58:03,710 --> 00:58:05,730
Get up! Get up!

447
00:58:06,940 --> 00:58:09,160
Come here! Osman!

448
00:58:09,330 --> 00:58:11,830
Surrender to Commander Kalonoz now!

449
00:58:12,030 --> 00:58:18,070
If you don't, Aygül's beautiful head
will be removed from her body!

450
00:58:18,710 --> 00:58:20,940
Move! Move!

451
00:58:24,250 --> 00:58:27,800
They may not call me Osman,
son of Ertuğrul anymore...

452
00:58:27,830 --> 00:58:30,500
... if I don't make
this castle their graves.

453
00:58:31,950 --> 00:58:36,420
- What are we going to do my Bey?
- Now is the time to take heads!

454
00:58:37,760 --> 00:58:40,740
We will make these lands
graves to those infidels!

455
00:58:41,220 --> 00:58:42,800
Listen to me carefully.

456
00:59:09,360 --> 00:59:11,080
My husband, Yorgopolos...

457
00:59:11,370 --> 00:59:17,540
Was not just a governor of this castle,
he was the protector of all of us.

458
00:59:20,240 --> 00:59:26,000
But we couldn't protect him, we've
lost him to a treacherous murder.

459
00:59:26,320 --> 00:59:28,980
We will arrange the funeral
ceremony tomorrow.

460
00:59:29,030 --> 00:59:31,700
Has everyone in the region been informed?

461
00:59:33,170 --> 00:59:35,310
Messengers are on their way, ma'am.

462
00:59:38,140 --> 00:59:43,100
This means the start of a
never-ending war with the Turks.

463
00:59:44,990 --> 00:59:48,570
Maximize the precautions
in the entire castle.

464
00:59:49,000 --> 00:59:54,080
Start working to find volunteers
to fight on our side.

465
00:59:55,460 --> 01:00:01,290
I can not even breathe before I take my
husband's revenge from the Turks.

466
01:00:27,650 --> 01:00:31,650
And you, Kalonoz,
I appoint you as my deputy.

467
01:00:34,850 --> 01:00:40,130
Also with the privilege of
using all the power that I have.

468
01:00:41,750 --> 01:00:44,520
I assure you that I will
be worthy of your trust.

469
01:00:46,390 --> 01:00:47,910
You can leave.

470
01:01:08,440 --> 01:01:12,440
Now, speak to me Kalonoz.

471
01:01:12,790 --> 01:01:16,130
What do you think you are doing?

472
01:01:16,390 --> 01:01:21,230
How dare you enter my tent and
kidnap my daughter, like a jackal?

473
01:01:22,650 --> 01:01:26,650
I'm Dündar Bey, son of Süleyman Şah!

474
01:01:27,400 --> 01:01:31,400
Who will protect you from my wrath?

475
01:01:32,290 --> 01:01:33,520
Who will?

476
01:01:34,270 --> 01:01:37,230
Your stone walls? Your iron doors?

477
01:01:37,670 --> 01:01:41,290
The soldiers you put behind those
doors? Who?

478
01:01:42,700 --> 01:01:45,910
Bring me my daughter, now!

479
01:01:46,180 --> 01:01:49,930
Are you threating me in
my own castle, Dündar Bey?

480
01:01:50,090 --> 01:01:55,070
Not in your castle, in the castle
of my friend Yorgopolos.

481
01:01:58,710 --> 01:02:04,370
I'm warning you, Kalonoz.
Threatening is for the weak.

482
01:02:04,750 --> 01:02:09,490
Is Yorgopolos, who I saw as a father, in
a coffin because he was your friend?

483
01:02:09,570 --> 01:02:14,560
Commander! If you have
something to say, say it right away.

484
01:02:16,210 --> 01:02:18,150
Don't mumble.

485
01:02:18,830 --> 01:02:20,760
Osman killed him.

486
01:02:21,660 --> 01:02:25,660
Osman, nephew of Dündar
Bey, friend of Yorgopolos!

487
01:02:30,020 --> 01:02:35,680
The governor would be in a coffin
earlier if we hadn't had Osman...

488
01:02:35,800 --> 01:02:37,940
... when we came for agreement.

489
01:02:38,470 --> 01:02:41,290
We know Osman is in the castle.

490
01:02:42,850 --> 01:02:47,470
If he is innocent, we would
like him to prove it.

491
01:02:48,410 --> 01:02:54,080
We would have done everything
to Aygül, if we had bad intentions.

492
01:02:55,140 --> 01:03:00,890
If you hurt Aygül, I'll burn Kulucahisar
to the ground.

493
01:03:01,710 --> 01:03:02,830
I'll burn it!

494
01:03:05,500 --> 01:03:07,730
Let me go!

495
01:03:08,430 --> 01:03:09,650
Move!

496
01:03:26,480 --> 01:03:27,990
Andreas!

497
01:03:28,630 --> 01:03:30,210
Let the lady go.

498
01:03:36,620 --> 01:03:40,000
My Aygül! My girl!

499
01:03:40,580 --> 01:03:44,060
Are you okay? Did they hurt you?

500
01:03:44,760 --> 01:03:46,770
I'm okay, father.

501
01:03:48,730 --> 01:03:51,850
These bastards don't
have the guts to touch me.

502
01:03:53,560 --> 01:03:56,830
If they had the guts, instead of
blaming Osman...

503
01:03:57,600 --> 01:04:00,820
...they would look for
the governor's killer.

504
01:04:01,640 --> 01:04:03,480
I trusted Osman.

505
01:04:04,700 --> 01:04:06,380
So did my husband.

506
01:04:07,470 --> 01:04:10,710
He granted him privileges no one had.

507
01:04:12,610 --> 01:04:16,360
My husband's killer is Osman, Aygül.

508
01:04:18,680 --> 01:04:20,730
There are witnesses!

509
01:04:22,130 --> 01:04:26,130
Osman! Unless Osman surrenders...

510
01:04:26,910 --> 01:04:32,220
... you, your father, Kayı's Beys,
no one gets out of this castle alive!

511
01:04:37,630 --> 01:04:39,520
- Kalonoz!
- Yes sir.

512
01:04:39,520 --> 01:04:43,930
Until Osman comes, put them all
in the dungeon.

513
01:04:46,000 --> 01:04:50,000
You've shown Byzantine's ugly face, Sofia.

514
01:04:50,430 --> 01:04:51,440
You've shown it.

515
01:04:51,650 --> 01:04:56,250
Are trying to use Osman as an excuse and
ruin our deal with the governor?

516
01:04:57,040 --> 01:05:00,890
Osman is not in this castle, we all
know that.

517
01:05:01,930 --> 01:05:06,520
I see, that it wasn't about Osman, it
was about me.

518
01:05:09,630 --> 01:05:13,450
If we get hurt...

519
01:05:14,180 --> 01:05:18,960
... all of the Turkish tents will be
your nightmare.

520
01:05:19,440 --> 01:05:20,490
Know that.

521
01:05:22,220 --> 01:05:27,190
If you'll burn the whole Kulucahisar for
a single hair of your daughter...

522
01:05:28,200 --> 01:05:32,700
...I'll kill all of the Turkish Tents for
a single drop of the governor's blood.

523
01:05:34,780 --> 01:05:38,400
-Take them out!
-Get them! All of them!

524
01:06:03,010 --> 01:06:04,390
Osman!

525
01:06:36,820 --> 01:06:40,540
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name
of Allah, the beneficent, the merciful)

526
01:06:40,860 --> 01:06:42,860
May it heal you.

527
01:06:46,020 --> 01:06:49,410
My Allah may your valiants be victorious
against the enemy.

528
01:06:49,410 --> 01:06:50,610
Amen.

529
01:06:51,490 --> 01:06:56,210
Inform all the women, all the Alps in
the Tent.

530
01:06:56,410 --> 01:06:59,810
Let the war begin. They must be prepared.

531
01:06:59,920 --> 01:07:02,470
We can make a move any second.

532
01:07:03,740 --> 01:07:07,220
Zöhre Hatun, will we get moving?

533
01:07:09,710 --> 01:07:12,180
We're Turkish women.

534
01:07:13,240 --> 01:07:16,720
We learned to fight from our men.

535
01:07:22,570 --> 01:07:27,170
You were making a lot of noise. Now
talk, Dündar Bey.

536
01:07:27,950 --> 01:07:30,490
You didn't believe Osman was in the
castle.

537
01:07:31,060 --> 01:07:35,190
Look, he's here with us, looking
like a warrior.

538
01:07:37,650 --> 01:07:39,720
I got what I wanted.

539
01:07:40,300 --> 01:07:42,970
I made Osman come into my lap.

540
01:07:43,070 --> 01:07:45,900
What came into your lap is death, Sofia.

541
01:07:47,380 --> 01:07:50,070
Let them go, or everyone dies.

542
01:07:51,940 --> 01:07:56,650
You killed my husband and lots of
my soldiers.

543
01:07:56,990 --> 01:07:58,940
Let him go!

544
01:08:02,310 --> 01:08:05,530
Isn't the blood you spilt enough for
you, Osman?

545
01:08:06,210 --> 01:08:08,510
I keep my promises.

546
01:08:10,120 --> 01:08:15,460
Without taking my nephew Osman with
me, I'm going nowhere. Know that.

547
01:08:15,850 --> 01:08:18,520
Relax, Dündar Bey.

548
01:08:19,270 --> 01:08:25,900
Osman will be on trial in a fair court,
with your judges in it.

549
01:08:26,420 --> 01:08:29,420
Kayı's Beys will also be in this court.

550
01:08:30,080 --> 01:08:34,800
We're after the truth, not spilling blood.

551
01:08:48,280 --> 01:08:52,770
Sofia is right, Dündar Bey.

552
01:08:58,900 --> 01:09:04,040
If we were in the same situation, we
would do the same.

553
01:09:05,740 --> 01:09:07,530
Bamsı Bey.

554
01:09:08,790 --> 01:09:11,330
Do you know what you're talking about?

555
01:09:12,630 --> 01:09:14,880
Where will we go without taking Osman?

556
01:09:27,130 --> 01:09:29,630
My heart is convinced.

557
01:09:31,920 --> 01:09:36,650
A fair court should be established
for everyone's good.

558
01:09:59,440 --> 01:10:03,120
Soldiers! Put your spears down.

559
01:10:19,960 --> 01:10:21,760
Osman!

560
01:10:24,600 --> 01:10:26,090
Uncle!

561
01:10:28,030 --> 01:10:29,820
Go.

562
01:10:32,400 --> 01:10:34,800
Bamsı Bey is right.

563
01:10:48,360 --> 01:10:51,640
Soldiers! Give Dündar Bey his weapons.

564
01:10:51,770 --> 01:10:55,000
And escort them to the exit.

565
01:10:55,160 --> 01:10:57,780
And take Osman to the dungeon.

566
01:11:32,380 --> 01:11:36,380
Osman has been caught! He's in the castle!
Hurry up, come on!

567
01:11:38,950 --> 01:11:43,530
-Hurry up, hurry!
-It's almost done. Keep your eyes open.

568
01:12:12,740 --> 01:12:16,740
Osman Bey! You couldn't protect your
brother!

569
01:12:16,950 --> 01:12:20,950
How could you let him die? How could you?

570
01:12:23,420 --> 01:12:28,110
Answer my questions! I don't care if you
saved me, I'll kill you!

571
01:12:28,800 --> 01:12:31,080
Did you kill the governor?

572
01:12:31,710 --> 01:12:34,600
What governor? What killing?

573
01:13:05,520 --> 01:13:07,590
Did you kill the governor?

574
01:13:13,220 --> 01:13:15,860
Shouldn't I be the one who's asking this?

575
01:13:15,980 --> 01:13:18,740
While I was saving Yorgopolos' life...

576
01:13:20,150 --> 01:13:25,390
... you were wandering around
as a useless castle commander.

577
01:13:28,530 --> 01:13:31,140
The assassination attempt was also
a trick, wasn't it?

578
01:13:33,340 --> 01:13:36,210
You Turks were behind this.

579
01:13:37,290 --> 01:13:43,390
Now tell me. What were you doing in the
governor's room disguised as a soldier?

580
01:13:43,680 --> 01:13:46,850
I entered the castle to look for the
ones who were trying to...

581
01:13:46,850 --> 01:13:48,550
... kill the governor and my uncle.

582
01:13:48,650 --> 01:13:50,550
But I was late.

583
01:13:51,510 --> 01:13:55,510
Besides, why would I kill the governor?

584
01:13:57,070 --> 01:13:59,220
He accepted the deal.

585
01:14:00,570 --> 01:14:04,290
You were the only one who didn't
accept it.

586
01:14:07,020 --> 01:14:11,570
If there is someone to be questioned,
it's you Kalonoz.

587
01:14:11,690 --> 01:14:13,790
Why did you kill our governor?

588
01:14:13,790 --> 01:14:17,770
While both the betrayal and the devilry
spreads from the castle you're...

589
01:14:17,770 --> 01:14:19,470
... commanding, are you blaming me?

590
01:14:19,760 --> 01:14:23,020
While you were escaping from the room
you killed the governor in...

591
01:14:23,020 --> 01:14:24,400
... my soldiers saw you.

592
01:14:26,260 --> 01:14:30,350
You're wrong, Kalonoz. Poor governor
fell in front of me.

593
01:14:32,790 --> 01:14:36,500
When I looked up, I saw two shadows.

594
01:14:37,690 --> 01:14:39,590
Shadows, huh.

595
01:14:41,860 --> 01:14:44,650
- So there were more than one.
- Yes.

596
01:14:47,330 --> 01:14:49,520
The governor was taken by surprise.

597
01:14:50,240 --> 01:14:55,840
If they can get that close to him, they
must be someone he knew.

598
01:14:56,880 --> 01:14:58,630
How do you know?

599
01:15:00,780 --> 01:15:03,040
Because he was drowned.

600
01:15:03,120 --> 01:15:05,800
Enough with your nonsense!

601
01:15:12,010 --> 01:15:14,910
You know I'm telling the truth.

602
01:15:17,830 --> 01:15:20,470
I'm not the killer.

603
01:15:21,390 --> 01:15:25,460
Everything will come to light in the
court.

604
01:15:26,400 --> 01:15:31,050
And with great pleasure, I'll rip your
head from your body.

605
01:15:32,060 --> 01:15:34,510
Osman Bey.

606
01:15:56,650 --> 01:15:59,600
I don't know what the court will decide.

607
01:16:00,650 --> 01:16:01,620
But...

608
01:16:03,320 --> 01:16:08,590
... you better believe, that I'll find
the killers.

609
01:16:13,490 --> 01:16:17,900
The dead, can't find anything.

610
01:16:20,290 --> 01:16:21,980
Osman.

611
01:16:27,320 --> 01:16:30,750
Lock the door, don't let anyone inside!

612
01:17:17,610 --> 01:17:19,450
You called me, Madam.

613
01:17:23,680 --> 01:17:28,130
You've thought this through. Osman will
only talk this way.

614
01:17:28,290 --> 01:17:30,470
We should remove his nails, teeth.

615
01:17:30,700 --> 01:17:33,520
He shall feel the pain.

616
01:17:33,690 --> 01:17:37,690
I don't think we can make Osman talk
by torturing him.

617
01:17:38,040 --> 01:17:41,180
-There is no other way, Madam.
-There is.

618
01:17:43,200 --> 01:17:47,100
If Osman managed to get the holy
entrustments...

619
01:17:47,110 --> 01:17:50,950
... he's collaborating with our biggest
enemy.

620
01:17:52,530 --> 01:17:56,310
Someone like him won't surrender
to pain, Helen.

621
01:17:56,310 --> 01:18:00,150
If Osman appears in court, governor's
death will be doubtful, Madam.

622
01:18:01,760 --> 01:18:05,640
-We can't let that happen.
-Osman won't appear in court, Helen.

623
01:18:05,640 --> 01:18:07,790
He'll escape from the dungeon.

624
01:18:09,120 --> 01:18:11,750
Will we get him out of the dungeon?

625
01:18:12,820 --> 01:18:15,510
No, he'll escape by himself.

626
01:18:15,760 --> 01:18:21,030
Osman is smart enough to take precaution
before surrendering.

627
01:18:24,390 --> 01:18:26,810
And he's not alone in the castle.

628
01:18:27,280 --> 01:18:30,430
It's impossible for him to take the
treasure alone.

629
01:18:31,240 --> 01:18:34,140
Do you think he got into the castle with
his Alps (men)?

630
01:18:36,050 --> 01:18:42,790
The smartest move to catch all of them
and get the holy entrustments...

631
01:18:43,420 --> 01:18:46,950
... is letting him escape from the dungeon.

632
01:18:48,280 --> 01:18:49,870
Now...

633
01:18:51,050 --> 01:18:55,570
Call my best hunter Teokres. Give orders
to him and his men.

634
01:18:55,570 --> 01:18:58,750
This is very dangerous! If Osman gets out
of Teokres' hands...

635
01:18:58,750 --> 01:19:02,750
... it will be impossible to get our hands
on the holy entrustments ever again!

636
01:19:02,880 --> 01:19:06,880
I'd prefer playing this risky game to
be punished....

637
01:19:07,630 --> 01:19:10,110
by Master Yannis, Helen.

638
01:19:10,670 --> 01:19:12,360
Now, do as I say!

639
01:19:12,910 --> 01:19:14,370
Go call Teokres!

640
01:19:37,090 --> 01:19:39,680
Put the barrels next to the others.

641
01:19:43,920 --> 01:19:47,170
The governor's killer's last
meal will be pig soup.

642
01:19:47,820 --> 01:19:49,980
Now that's funny!

643
01:19:51,220 --> 01:19:53,280
Bring me the soup bowl.

644
01:19:59,650 --> 01:20:01,540
A little more.

645
01:20:03,530 --> 01:20:07,030
Put more meat, he should eat it
nicely before dying.

646
01:20:15,610 --> 01:20:17,570
What are you looking at?

647
01:20:18,050 --> 01:20:21,440
Isn't the killer Muslim? He won't
drink that soup.

648
01:20:22,880 --> 01:20:26,170
That's the fun part. Mind your own
business.

649
01:20:26,170 --> 01:20:30,530
There's no getting out of hell for him.
Besides, where else would a Turk go?

650
01:20:51,710 --> 01:20:53,900
Come on, do your job.

651
01:21:11,950 --> 01:21:13,530
Get out.

652
01:21:44,370 --> 01:21:48,130
- Teokres!
- You called me, Helen.

653
01:21:57,580 --> 01:22:02,660
I remember the day Princess Sofia took
your eye out with her one finger.

654
01:22:06,520 --> 01:22:13,120
If you want to keep the other one, listen
to me carefully, Teokres!

655
01:22:30,080 --> 01:22:34,080
If an Alp (man) doesn't care about
the Kayı's honour...

656
01:22:35,180 --> 01:22:37,440
... why would he need a headgear for?

657
01:22:55,350 --> 01:23:00,650
What's the use of a sword if it's not
used for pride, honour.

658
01:23:03,300 --> 01:23:06,020
You don't need those either.

659
01:23:16,020 --> 01:23:20,020
We entrusted our martyr Aybars' fiance...

660
01:23:21,020 --> 01:23:24,580
... and my sister Aygül.

661
01:23:26,490 --> 01:23:28,840
And what did you do?

662
01:23:30,460 --> 01:23:33,600
What did you do? Tell me!

663
01:23:36,610 --> 01:23:39,920
You couldn't protect them.

664
01:23:44,940 --> 01:23:48,080
You didn't hear a thing while my sister
was being kidnapped.

665
01:23:49,900 --> 01:23:53,990
Being a Kayı Alp means to guard
like a hawk!

666
01:23:54,520 --> 01:23:58,030
It means being a warrior who accepts death
for honour!

667
01:24:01,380 --> 01:24:05,080
The one who can't protect entrustments,
who can't protect their honour...

668
01:24:05,490 --> 01:24:07,790
... neither deserves being an Alp, nor
the sword!

669
01:24:09,850 --> 01:24:15,250
But I'll give you what you
deserve, don't you worry.

670
01:24:23,000 --> 01:24:27,920
Dündar Bey, you'd sacrifice yourself and
still wouldn't leave Osman to them.

671
01:24:28,170 --> 01:24:29,710
So why did you?

672
01:24:29,910 --> 01:24:32,630
You can't put an eagle in a cage, Hatun.

673
01:24:33,220 --> 01:24:34,730
It won't fit.

674
01:24:40,430 --> 01:24:44,590
-Tell them, Bamsı Bey.
-Thank you, Dündar Bey.

675
01:24:46,840 --> 01:24:52,330
Zöhre Hatun, if it weren't for Osman, we
wouldn't be here.

676
01:25:20,610 --> 01:25:24,390
He was plotting something, so
I said nothing.

677
01:25:30,120 --> 01:25:34,070
Nonetheless, I'll take precautions.

678
01:25:34,070 --> 01:25:38,860
Bamsı Bey, after all this pain, will we
still be thankful of Osman?

679
01:25:40,430 --> 01:25:44,830
Not only his own but also yours, my
father's, Samsa Bey's, my sister's...

680
01:25:44,830 --> 01:25:46,450
... everyone's life is in danger.

681
01:25:46,640 --> 01:25:48,650
For how long will this go on?

682
01:25:49,000 --> 01:25:51,640
What if he's found guilty in the court?

683
01:25:52,970 --> 01:25:55,440
What if he actually killed the governor?

684
01:25:56,660 --> 01:25:59,070
I don't take any excuses.

685
01:26:01,330 --> 01:26:05,330
I say we make Osman pay for all of this.
Because...

686
01:26:05,570 --> 01:26:10,510
... if Osman's found guilty for the murder
Seljuk Sultan will make us pay for it.

687
01:26:10,510 --> 01:26:12,580
Enough brother, enough!

688
01:26:12,580 --> 01:26:15,200
You never stop praising Osman.

689
01:26:15,200 --> 01:26:19,150
My sister, my father you say but,
Osman sacrificed...

690
01:26:19,150 --> 01:26:21,480
... himself for your sister and your
father!

691
01:26:21,480 --> 01:26:23,580
- Aygül!
- Batur!

692
01:26:51,870 --> 01:26:53,810
Batur is right.

693
01:26:54,690 --> 01:26:57,990
If Osman's found guilty in the court...

694
01:26:59,470 --> 01:27:02,630
... Byzantium won't let this one go.

695
01:27:03,280 --> 01:27:08,720
What if they don't, Dündar Bey? When were
we afraid of Byzantium?

696
01:27:09,370 --> 01:27:12,710
It's not about the Byzantium, Bamsı Bey.

697
01:27:13,900 --> 01:27:18,610
If Byzantium is involved in this, the
Mongolians will also be.

698
01:27:20,640 --> 01:27:24,560
My father must return to his
Tent as soon as possible.

699
01:27:26,070 --> 01:27:30,400
Allah willing, if he comes to terms with
the Sultan in Konya...

700
01:27:30,400 --> 01:27:33,690
... this matter will be sorted out.
- Allah willing!

701
01:29:33,260 --> 01:29:37,990
What is it, didn't you like it? These are
your last meals, Osman Bey.

702
01:29:38,380 --> 01:29:42,890
Enjoy them. The pig inside will
carry you to heaven.

703
01:30:21,980 --> 01:30:23,740
You bastard!

704
01:32:28,500 --> 01:32:32,970
Who entered the dungeon last? Who
entered this dungeon last?

705
01:32:33,310 --> 01:32:34,750
Helen.

706
01:32:43,520 --> 01:32:48,480
Shut the doors, catch Osman.
He will not leave this castle alive!

707
01:32:53,450 --> 01:32:55,090
Sofia...

708
01:33:22,480 --> 01:33:25,060
Mother earth...

709
01:33:27,460 --> 01:33:31,460
Tell me, tell me mother earth.

710
01:33:32,110 --> 01:33:34,890
Is the valiant inside you comfortable?

711
01:33:37,580 --> 01:33:42,830
Is he far from his father, from his Tent?

712
01:33:51,560 --> 01:33:57,700
May our creator not make us
seek help from the cowards.

713
01:33:58,470 --> 01:34:00,770
May your white-haired mother rest
in peace.

714
01:34:00,770 --> 01:34:02,470
Rest in peace.
May your white-haired mother rest
in peace.

715
01:34:02,470 --> 01:34:02,660
Rest in peace.

716
01:34:04,270 --> 01:34:05,770
May my Allah...

717
01:34:06,270 --> 01:34:08,080
never leave you without faith.

718
01:34:10,780 --> 01:34:15,110
Those who say "Amin" may see Allah.

719
01:34:17,870 --> 01:34:20,550
May the hope that Allah gives
you never be given up.

720
01:34:23,500 --> 01:34:25,090
May Allah forgive your sins...

721
01:34:27,280 --> 01:34:31,280
for the sake of Muhammad...

722
01:34:32,820 --> 01:34:34,350
whose name is precious.

723
01:34:58,790 --> 01:35:00,210
My Aybars.

724
01:35:02,100 --> 01:35:05,840
Don't worry about anything, my Aybars.

725
01:35:07,650 --> 01:35:11,880
My Osman will take revenge for you.

726
01:35:14,300 --> 01:35:15,500
My Osman...

727
01:35:16,700 --> 01:35:20,120
will take revenge for you.

728
01:35:54,300 --> 01:35:58,810
You couldn't share the food more unfairly,
brother.

729
01:36:05,880 --> 01:36:07,250
Now...

730
01:36:08,040 --> 01:36:10,660
we're one step closer to the
truth, brothers.

731
01:36:11,110 --> 01:36:14,830
-The tangle will be untangled by the nun.
-Thank you, my Bey, thank you.

732
01:36:15,350 --> 01:36:16,730
Inshaallah, my Bey.

733
01:36:26,880 --> 01:36:28,370
Protect Osman Bey!

734
01:36:45,400 --> 01:36:46,600
Konuralp.

735
01:36:54,550 --> 01:36:56,900
-Salaam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salaam.

736
01:36:56,930 --> 01:36:58,580
Alaikum Salaam.

737
01:37:07,920 --> 01:37:11,260
I learned that you were in the
castle. I came to see you.

738
01:37:11,370 --> 01:37:13,630
I know you're friendly, Konuralp.

739
01:37:14,270 --> 01:37:17,890
If I say that we're going to
die, you'll come anyway.

740
01:37:20,450 --> 01:37:21,540
Come to our table.

741
01:37:21,800 --> 01:37:23,280
With pleasure, my Bey.

742
01:37:33,320 --> 01:37:34,760
Did you do your duty?

743
01:37:35,050 --> 01:37:36,420
Of course, my Bey.

744
01:37:46,760 --> 01:37:50,650
All the castles' private structures in
Vitinya are done, my Bey.

745
01:37:51,080 --> 01:37:52,650
Mashallah.

746
01:37:53,570 --> 01:37:57,380
We have the distance between the walls...

747
01:37:57,850 --> 01:38:00,100
the number of soldiers
who protect the walls...

748
01:38:00,120 --> 01:38:01,960
and the height of the walls.

749
01:38:02,200 --> 01:38:05,790
- We have everyting.
- I am proud of you, Konuralp

750
01:38:07,360 --> 01:38:08,660
Thanks, my Bey.

751
01:38:08,860 --> 01:38:11,790
We'll open the gates of
holy wars again.

752
01:38:12,330 --> 01:38:16,950
And we'll name the lands that we conquer
after the brave conquerors.

753
01:38:17,460 --> 01:38:18,780
Inshaallah, my Bey.

754
01:38:19,310 --> 01:38:22,650
With Allah's permission, the places we
set foot in will be the land...

755
01:38:23,180 --> 01:38:26,410
and those places will be a
magnificent land that...

756
01:38:27,080 --> 01:38:29,270
people shelter.

757
01:38:32,830 --> 01:38:33,880
But first...

758
01:38:34,830 --> 01:38:37,450
we'll take revenge for my brother Aybars.

759
01:38:38,040 --> 01:38:39,290
From now on...

760
01:38:39,400 --> 01:38:41,730
it doesn't matter if
a basilisk we'll confront...

761
01:38:41,800 --> 01:38:44,640
becomes a dragon with seven heads.

762
01:38:47,590 --> 01:38:48,810
Be quiet.

763
01:38:48,820 --> 01:38:50,690
Osman should be here.

764
01:39:05,510 --> 01:39:06,840
We found their traces.

765
01:39:07,860 --> 01:39:10,470
I don't want any crunch. Be careful.

766
01:39:34,310 --> 01:39:36,970
-May it be the cure, father.
-Thanks, daughter.

767
01:39:39,370 --> 01:39:41,690
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(in the name of Allah)

768
01:39:51,080 --> 01:39:55,700
We need to find Osman and build a
court before things get crazy.

769
01:39:56,260 --> 01:39:59,570
Or else, they'll stir up
Byzantine and Seljuq...

770
01:39:59,620 --> 01:40:03,150
thinking that he's the killer
of the Governor.

771
01:40:05,640 --> 01:40:08,150
Let's see how much trouble he'll cause.

772
01:40:10,810 --> 01:40:12,510
Can I come in, my Bey?

773
01:40:13,550 --> 01:40:15,120
Come in.

774
01:40:19,670 --> 01:40:22,290
Osman Bey got out of the castle
safe and sound, my Bey.

775
01:40:22,310 --> 01:40:24,590
One of his alps let me know.

776
01:40:29,190 --> 01:40:32,980
-Where's Osman's man now?
-He's gone, my Bey.

777
01:40:39,440 --> 01:40:43,120
Batur, if Osman's man is
around, follow him.

778
01:40:43,190 --> 01:40:46,240
Find Osman wherever he is.

779
01:41:15,590 --> 01:41:17,770
Turk friend Yogopolos...

780
01:41:17,910 --> 01:41:20,200
was a huge embarrassment for us.

781
01:41:30,270 --> 01:41:34,420
Kulucahisar is a real
Christian castle now.

782
01:41:40,600 --> 01:41:43,690
They must be around. We'll trap him.

783
01:41:57,130 --> 01:41:58,470
Eternal Allah!

784
01:41:58,980 --> 01:42:00,520
Eternal Allah!

785
01:42:25,960 --> 01:42:29,660
A coyote falls into the wolf's paw!

786
01:43:15,900 --> 01:43:18,200
Who sent you?

787
01:43:20,130 --> 01:43:21,460
Tell me.

788
01:43:31,870 --> 01:43:33,030
Talk to me!

789
01:43:42,150 --> 01:43:43,950
No! Not my eyes!

790
01:43:43,990 --> 01:43:46,370
Stop, stop! No! Not my eyes!

791
01:43:46,420 --> 01:43:48,680
-Not my eyes!
-Talk to me.

792
01:43:48,830 --> 01:43:50,980
Talk and I'll spare your life and eyes.

793
01:43:51,110 --> 01:43:54,680
Stop! Stop, okay! I'll tell you.

794
01:43:54,860 --> 01:43:55,890
-I'll tell you.
-Talk.

795
01:43:56,110 --> 01:43:58,950
I'll tell you! Stop!

796
01:43:59,670 --> 01:44:02,000
Sofia! Sofia!

797
01:44:02,900 --> 01:44:04,730
Princess Sofia!

798
01:44:16,300 --> 01:44:19,120
We'll hide this bastard.

799
01:44:20,040 --> 01:44:21,240
Boran.

800
01:44:22,000 --> 01:44:24,240
Hide him in your secret place.

801
01:44:27,930 --> 01:44:29,450
Okay, my Bey.

802
01:44:36,940 --> 01:44:37,910
My Bey.

803
01:44:38,420 --> 01:44:41,010
Why did Sofia send a man after you?

804
01:44:41,400 --> 01:44:44,230
She knew that I didn't kill
her master, Konuralp.

805
01:44:45,800 --> 01:44:47,270
It's not about me.

806
01:44:48,280 --> 01:44:50,610
It's about the nuns who have
saved me in the bog.

807
01:44:50,680 --> 01:44:52,820
She doesn't know about the nuns, my Bey.

808
01:44:53,140 --> 01:44:54,750
You've just told me.

809
01:44:54,840 --> 01:44:58,840
Whatever the nuns have to do with
her, she thinks that it's about me.

810
01:44:59,290 --> 01:45:01,760
So, she sent her bastards after me.

811
01:45:02,800 --> 01:45:04,760
If we find the nuns...

812
01:45:05,810 --> 01:45:08,720
we'll find the answers of many questions.

813
01:46:08,180 --> 01:46:12,800
We thought that they wouldn't find us
but they came closer to us.

814
01:46:13,940 --> 01:46:15,530
Sir...

815
01:46:15,950 --> 01:46:19,370
-how did they find the treasure?
-We'll learn that from Osman.

816
01:46:19,490 --> 01:46:21,720
Bring him to me.

817
01:46:24,950 --> 01:46:26,580
Master Yannis...

818
01:46:27,120 --> 01:46:29,730
Sofia let Osman escape from the dungeon...

819
01:46:30,680 --> 01:46:33,370
to reach the holy entrustments.

820
01:46:34,540 --> 01:46:38,020
-Who did she send after Osman?
-Teokres, sir.

821
01:47:23,120 --> 01:47:25,920
The most important
teachers in the world...

822
01:47:26,610 --> 01:47:28,710
are the pains.

823
01:47:30,730 --> 01:47:33,620
Now tell me...

824
01:47:35,290 --> 01:47:37,320
where is the...

825
01:47:38,460 --> 01:47:40,310
stolen...

826
01:47:42,670 --> 01:47:44,060
treasure?

827
01:47:47,670 --> 01:47:49,420
Where's Sofia?

828
01:47:50,350 --> 01:47:52,610
She knows that you're here, sir.

829
01:47:54,710 --> 01:47:56,360
She's about to come.

830
01:48:14,000 --> 01:48:16,330
How will we explain this to Master Yannis?

831
01:48:16,600 --> 01:48:17,730
I don't know.

832
01:48:17,780 --> 01:48:20,290
But Master Yannis will be so pissed off.

833
01:48:29,230 --> 01:48:31,100
Where are you going, Sofia?

834
01:48:32,120 --> 01:48:34,740
What are you up to? It's time to find out.

835
01:49:03,440 --> 01:49:05,030
Osman Bey!

836
01:49:11,020 --> 01:49:12,410
Alper!

837
01:49:31,010 --> 01:49:33,050
You shoot too many arrows!

838
01:49:33,620 --> 01:49:35,780
You appear without weapons.

839
01:49:36,500 --> 01:49:38,770
Are you a friend of a foe?

840
01:49:38,890 --> 01:49:40,050
Who are you?

841
01:49:40,210 --> 01:49:43,770
We are the punishers for cruels,
and the helpers for innocents, son.

842
01:49:44,460 --> 01:49:47,260
Our duty is to take you to
what you search for.

843
01:50:08,220 --> 01:50:10,060
Now you masquerade as Turk.

844
01:50:12,240 --> 01:50:16,240
You're so brave, Osman Bey! You've
come all the way for your curiosity.

845
01:50:16,270 --> 01:50:19,540
Not for my curiosity. For my revenge.

846
01:50:20,710 --> 01:50:22,330
Tell me.

847
01:50:22,960 --> 01:50:26,080
Who are you? Why do you hide yourselves?

848
01:50:26,220 --> 01:50:29,310
If you want to find out, come with me.

849
01:50:30,490 --> 01:50:34,150
-Whatever your secret is, tell me now.
-I can't answer your questions.

850
01:50:35,080 --> 01:50:37,590
If you want to know, follow me.

851
01:50:39,850 --> 01:50:42,240
If you don't want the truth,
go to your way.

852
01:50:43,750 --> 01:50:47,100
But we have to go alone.

853
01:50:47,780 --> 01:50:49,570
Tell your men.

854
01:50:49,750 --> 01:50:52,050
They should wait here with Akçaderviş.

855
01:50:57,130 --> 01:50:58,210
My Alps. (men)

856
01:50:59,220 --> 01:51:01,090
Wait here.

857
01:52:13,900 --> 01:52:15,430
Master Yannis...

858
01:52:17,230 --> 01:52:19,510
I couldn't protect the secret, sir.

859
01:52:32,720 --> 01:52:35,820
It's your honor to make me pay the price.

860
01:53:26,890 --> 01:53:29,740
They infiltrated into us, Sofia.

861
01:53:30,800 --> 01:53:33,660
There is a spy in Margalit Monastery.

862
01:53:34,140 --> 01:53:36,600
We should learn who it is.

863
01:53:36,910 --> 01:53:41,300
-How is that possible?
- I came here to take back the holy entrustments.

864
01:53:43,060 --> 01:53:45,440
Not to kill you.

865
01:53:47,240 --> 01:53:48,340
Sofia!

866
01:53:52,240 --> 01:53:54,010
What's happening here?

867
01:54:00,480 --> 01:54:02,570
What are you doing here, Andreas?

868
01:54:03,130 --> 01:54:07,130
You're my most loyal aide. What
the are you doing here?

869
01:54:09,170 --> 01:54:11,710
What's happening in here, Sofia?

870
01:54:12,290 --> 01:54:14,340
Ensheathe your sword.

871
01:54:14,970 --> 01:54:17,550
-I have things to tell you.
-Now!

872
01:54:17,580 --> 01:54:20,370
You'll tell me now!

873
01:54:20,380 --> 01:54:22,770
Right now!

874
01:54:23,140 --> 01:54:24,550
Soldiers!

875
01:54:24,740 --> 01:54:27,060
Arrest Sofia and the rest!

876
01:54:28,970 --> 01:54:31,030
Release your sword, Commander Kalonoz.

877
01:54:34,250 --> 01:54:36,300
Release your sword.

878
01:55:14,820 --> 01:55:16,740
Welcome, Master Nizamettin.

879
01:55:25,650 --> 01:55:28,590
You haven't paid the tribute tax
for a while, Master Hasan.

880
01:55:29,150 --> 01:55:32,260
Tell me, do you deserve this stall?

881
01:55:34,960 --> 01:55:37,250
Do you see this bazaar?

882
01:55:37,760 --> 01:55:41,570
If I don't get tribute taxes on time, how
can I provide a regulation?

883
01:55:41,900 --> 01:55:43,810
I don't need an explanation.

884
01:55:48,070 --> 01:55:51,150
If he doesn't pay his tribute tax
tomorrow, scatter his stall.

885
01:56:08,180 --> 01:56:09,460
He's Osman.

886
01:57:59,670 --> 01:58:01,850
You wanted the truth, Osman Bey.

887
01:58:03,320 --> 01:58:04,590
Here you are.

888
01:58:49,890 --> 01:58:52,080
You're about to learn the truth.

889
01:58:53,730 --> 01:58:57,140
Now you can meet our leader and find
the answers to your questions.

890
01:58:57,520 --> 01:58:59,090
Who's your leader?

891
01:58:59,840 --> 01:59:01,600
Open the door of the secret.

892
01:59:01,890 --> 01:59:03,770
You can see with your eyes.

893
01:59:47,600 --> 01:59:49,760
Who am I meeting?

894
02:00:14,430 --> 02:00:17,070
We're the pilgrims of Allah.

895
02:00:20,750 --> 02:00:24,390
We're told our names as our faith.

896
02:00:27,180 --> 02:00:31,110
People know me as "Edebalı."

897
02:00:32,330 --> 02:00:33,660
Edebalı.

898
02:00:40,030 --> 02:00:41,600
The friend of my father.

899
02:00:44,190 --> 02:00:46,500
The light of Oğuz.

900
02:00:53,290 --> 02:00:56,250
I couldn't get the honor to see your face.

901
02:00:58,580 --> 02:01:00,400
Thank Allah.

902
02:01:14,200 --> 02:01:15,870
A Bey doesn't bow...

903
02:01:17,270 --> 02:01:20,310
before someone, son.

904
02:01:47,090 --> 02:01:48,060
Who's she?

905
02:01:48,640 --> 02:01:51,420
My daughter, Bala Hatun.
The head of sisters.

906
02:01:53,610 --> 02:01:57,610
The girl you see with her
is the friend of my daughter, Gonca.

907
02:01:58,940 --> 02:02:02,940
Master Priest is one of our friends.
He is Tursun.

908
02:02:06,880 --> 02:02:10,090
There are many things that aren't
like the way it seems.

909
02:02:12,120 --> 02:02:14,140
White becomes black...

910
02:02:14,590 --> 02:02:17,280
and black becomes white that...

911
02:02:17,320 --> 02:02:19,170
its mystery is beyond the mind.

912
02:02:19,730 --> 02:02:22,130
Mystery is the work of
wise people like you.

913
02:02:23,490 --> 02:02:26,160
I'm looking for the killers
of my brother Aybars.

914
02:02:28,370 --> 02:02:30,190
I know from my father.

915
02:02:30,590 --> 02:02:32,240
I know you from Kırşehir.

916
02:02:33,280 --> 02:02:35,040
What are you doing here?

917
02:02:35,550 --> 02:02:37,150
Why are you here?

918
02:02:37,260 --> 02:02:39,070
We're here...

919
02:02:40,200 --> 02:02:43,120
to blow the Yesevi breath.

920
02:02:44,960 --> 02:02:49,200
To fire the resurrection up, to
flare our tent up...

921
02:02:50,210 --> 02:02:52,720
to build new land.

922
02:02:55,690 --> 02:02:57,700
Do you want to join us...

923
02:02:58,050 --> 02:03:00,490
in this holy way?

924
02:03:07,670 --> 02:03:09,380
I do.

925
02:03:13,250 --> 02:03:14,660
But...

926
02:03:14,820 --> 02:03:16,020
I have a condition.

927
02:03:18,720 --> 02:03:21,390
I want to know all the secrets.

928
02:03:23,610 --> 02:03:26,980
Then, listen to me carefully.

929
02:03:33,840 --> 02:03:44,630
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com